    subgraph da_SRC["Desktop shell, daemon, installer and updates · desktop-app.mmd"]
      direction TB
        da_WHY["Windows first. The window is a viewer. harnessd owns the build<br/>A utility process would die with the Electron shell, so the daemon<br/>is detached and runs the Electron binary as plain Node<br/>A named pipe for the current user, plus a session token:<br/>no localhost port, so a web page cannot reach it<br/>Not a Windows Service: Git config, the vault and plan logins<br/>belong to the user. One daemon per Windows user"] --> da_PROC["Window: chat, canvas, cockpit, office. A crash reopens and reconnects<br/>Electron main: tray, notifications, updates. The daemon keeps running<br/>harnessd: coordinator per project, state.db, global broker,<br/>adapters, MCP, sandbox launcher, MinGit, verifier, doc fetcher<br/>Workers and verifiers: one attempt each. A crash returns to the checkpoint"]
        da_PROC --> da_CLOSE{"Close the window?"}
        da_CLOSE -->|Idle| da_QUIT["The app quits. The daemon stops after a short grace period"]
        da_CLOSE -->|Building| da_TRAY["Hide to the tray. First time: still building, N workers<br/>Tray: Open, Pause all, status, Quit"]
        da_TRAY --> da_QUITASK{"Quit while building?"}
        da_QUITASK -->|Pause and quit| da_PARK["Checkpoint everything, about 10 seconds, then quit"]
        da_QUITASK -->|Keep building| da_TRAY
        da_QUITASK -->|Cancel| da_TRAY
        da_PROC --> da_POWER["Sleep: pause dispatch, reconcile on wake. In-flight calls are unknown<br/>Shutdown or sign-out: checkpoint inside the shutdown window<br/>Anything missed resumes from the previous turn boundary<br/>Prevent sleep while building is off by default<br/>Start at sign-in is optional, for resumes after a plan window resets<br/>A second launch focuses the existing window"]
        da_POWER --> da_INST["Installer, about 200 MB: Electron, daemon, UI, MinGit,<br/>gitleaks, tree-sitter grammars, office art<br/>On demand, size shown, SHA-256 from a signed manifest:<br/>Whisper at first mic use. Playwright browsers at first browser tests<br/>Node, pnpm or Python if the project needs them and they are missing<br/>Ollama, LM Studio, Docker and WSL2 are never bundled<br/>A bad checksum is refused. Downloads resume. Any component can be removed"]
        da_INST --> da_UPD{"What is updating?"}
        da_UPD -->|The app| da_APP["Signed differential download in the background<br/>Restart to update only after every task is parked<br/>A live build says: applies after this build, or when you choose"]
        da_UPD -->|The database| da_DB["user_version on each SQLite file<br/>1 Park work, exclusive lock, VACUUM INTO a backup<br/>2 Forward-only migrations. Additive directly; constraint changes<br/>use SQLite's 12-step rebuild, then search indexes rebuild<br/>3 quick_check and invariants. On failure, restore the backup<br/>global.db first. Each project migrates on open; a failure marks<br/>only that project needs repair. Hourly and daily backups too<br/>Corruption: salvage, or restore, then replay harness-state and Git<br/>An older app cannot open a newer database. It offers the backup"]
        da_UPD -->|Parked work| da_OLD["Resume with the prompt and skill versions the task started with<br/>New versions apply to the next attempt<br/>Old checkpoint formats are upcast on read, never rewritten in place"]
        da_UPD -->|Provider policy| da_POL["Signed JSON, checked daily. New dispatches use the new file<br/>Only a revoked route parks running work, at the next boundary"]
        da_UPD -->|A foreign CLI| da_CLI["Its own installer. A new version runs the conformance suite<br/>before that runtime gets new tasks"]
        da_APP --> da_STACK
        da_DB --> da_STACK
        da_OLD --> da_STACK
        da_POL --> da_STACK
        da_CLI --> da_STACK["Electron, React, TypeScript, React Flow, ELK, PixiJS<br/>Daemon on the bundled Node. SQLite via node:sqlite, FTS5,<br/>better-sqlite3 only as fallback. Git is MinGit, not a library<br/>ACP, MCP and vendor SDKs. Playwright. NSIS via electron-builder, signed<br/>Electron and Node versions move together, checked in CI"]
        da_STACK --> da_DIAG["Logs, traces and crash dumps stay on this PC. Nothing is sent<br/>JSON logs for 14 days, secrets redacted before they are written<br/>A span per transaction, attempt, model call, tool, Git op and verification<br/>Health page: queues, rate limits, latency, verifier time, sandbox denials<br/>Help, Export diagnostics: a redacted bundle, previewed before it is saved"]
        da_DIAG --> da_EDGE["Two Windows users: separate daemon, pipe, data and sandbox identities<br/>Daemon still on the old version: park, exit, start the new one<br/>Disk: warn at 15 GB, no new dispatch at 5 GB, Pause all at 2 GB<br/>Antivirus quarantine: name the file, re-download and verify<br/>Moving the data folder: park, move, repair worktree paths"]
    end
    subgraph wg_SRC["Folder, Git, worktrees, and an existing codebase · workspace-git-and-brownfield.mmd"]
      direction TB
        wg_GIT["Git is required, and bundled as MinGit, so nothing is installed<br/>Parallel work, checkpoints, undo, export as branches and<br/>crash recovery are Git features. Plain copies, Jujutsu and<br/>per-file editor snapshots do not replace them in v1<br/>Mercurial or Perforce: not supported. Offer Work on a copy"] --> wg_PICK["Developer picks a folder. The checkout is their desk<br/>The harness never edits, stashes, resets or commits there<br/>without an explicit click"]
        wg_PICK --> wg_STATE{"What is in the folder?"}
        wg_STATE -->|Empty| wg_EMPTY["Silent git init, branch main<br/>The Phase 0 commit is scanned before it is made"]
        wg_STATE -->|Files, no Git| wg_NOGIT{"Set up Git, or work on a copy?<br/>There is no continue-without-Git"}
        wg_NOGIT -->|Set up Git here| wg_SCAN
        wg_NOGIT -->|Work on a copy| wg_COPY["Copy into a new folder and set up Git there"]
        wg_STATE -->|Clean repo| wg_CLEAN["Record HEAD and the branch as the project base"]
        wg_STATE -->|Uncommitted files| wg_DIRTY{"You have uncommitted files"}
        wg_DIRTY -->|Include my changes| wg_SCAN
        wg_DIRTY -->|Start from my last commit| wg_LAST["Warn that landing may later need those files committed"]
        wg_DIRTY -->|Let me commit first| wg_RECHECK["Wait, then recheck"]
        wg_STATE -->|No commits yet| wg_UNBORN["No commits yet. The baseline is shown before it is made"]
        wg_UNBORN --> wg_SCAN
        wg_STATE -->|Anything else| wg_OTHER["Merge, rebase, cherry-pick or conflicts: block.<br/>Open in my editor. Never finish or abort it<br/>Detached HEAD: pick a branch, or create harness-base and the date<br/>OneDrive, Dropbox or a network folder: warn, continue or move<br/>No user.name or email: one prompt, globals prefilled<br/>Git missing from PATH: the bundled Git is used"]
        wg_SCAN["Before any baseline or snapshot: scan .env files, private keys,<br/>high-entropy tokens, files over 50 MB, node_modules, build<br/>output and OS junk. Show the .gitignore proposal and the<br/>secrets that will not be committed. Accept, edit or cancel"] --> wg_COMMIT{"What is being recorded?"}
        wg_COMMIT -->|A first Git history| wg_BASE["Show what the baseline commit includes, then make it"]
        wg_COMMIT -->|Uncommitted work to include| wg_SNAP["Dirty work is snapshotted, never moved. Stash is not used<br/>Temporary index: GIT_INDEX_FILE, read-tree HEAD, add -A,<br/>write-tree, commit-tree with parent HEAD,<br/>store refs/harness/snapshots, then drop the temp index<br/>Working tree, real index and branch stay untouched<br/>The scan runs on the snapshot diff first. That commit is the workers' base<br/>A later identical developer commit merges cleanly"]
        wg_COPY --> wg_SCAN
        wg_BASE --> wg_REFS
        wg_EMPTY --> wg_REFS
        wg_CLEAN --> wg_REFS
        wg_LAST --> wg_REFS
        wg_RECHECK --> wg_REFS
        wg_OTHER --> wg_REFS
        wg_SNAP --> wg_REFS
        wg_REFS["Developer's branch: landing target, only by a visible landing<br/>harness/integration: accepted, tested work<br/>harness/f/feature: private while its tasks land<br/>harness/t/task/attempt: one leased attempt<br/>refs/harness/checkpoints: WIP, kept for resume and export<br/>Author is the role and agent id. Committer is the developer<br/>Trailers: Harness-Task, Harness-Attempt<br/>A human fix keeps the human as author"] --> wg_WT["Worktree outside the project, under LOCALAPPDATA<br/>git worktree add --detach, then the attempt branch<br/>core.longpaths. Registered on the attempt lease<br/>Ignored files are absent, so the environment manifest supplies them<br/>Secrets: env from the vault, never files<br/>Local config: an allowlist copy. Dependencies: the lockfile,<br/>with a shared package cache. Submodules init. LFS only for<br/>the task's paths. Sparse checkout when the brief declares it<br/>After retention: remove the worktree and prune<br/>Checkpoint refs survive until the feature lands or the user deletes them"]
        wg_WT --> wg_WIN["Windows: short worktree root. Optional Defender exclusion<br/>Keep .gitattributes, or the developer's autocrlf<br/>Workers never rewrite line endings<br/>Flag two paths that differ only by case<br/>Stop the attempt's Job Object before deleting a locked tree<br/>Predict a landing with git merge-tree --write-tree, before touching anything"]
        wg_WIN --> wg_OPEN{"Existing repo, or a new one?"}
        wg_OPEN -->|New| wg_DONE["Folder is ready. Discovery uses the opening prompts"]
        wg_OPEN -->|Existing| wg_CARD["Opening card from a local scan. Zero tokens spent<br/>What would you like to change?"]
        wg_CARD --> wg_LAYERS["Read cheaply, ask the model last<br/>L0, free: tree, languages, manifests, scripts, tests, CI,<br/>docs, schema, migrations, .env.example names, Git churn<br/>L1, free and local: tree-sitter symbols, reference graph,<br/>entry points from routes, main and bin<br/>L2, bounded and cached by blob hash: one module card<br/>per area this request touches. Show the estimate first<br/>L3, per task: exact files or spans at the pinned commit<br/>The message chooses the L2 modules. The rest stay at L0 or L1<br/>L0 and L1 never leave the machine. Mask secrets before L2<br/>A local-only project uses a local model, or skips L2"]
