    subgraph is_SRC["Mystery bugs and repo-wide sweeps · investigations-and-sweeps.mmd"]
      direction TB
        is_KIND{"Known write scope?"}
        is_KIND -->|No. A symptom, unknown files| is_INV
        is_KIND -->|Many files, one change| is_SWEEP
        is_INV["Investigation. Read widely. Write almost nothing<br/>1 Intake: symptom card. Ask the missing facts once<br/>2 Reproduce: tests/repro only. Fail for the reported reason,<br/>in a clean environment. Repeat to measure flakes<br/>3 Localize: temporary logs on a quarantined branch<br/>4 Prove: a second model checks the note. A minimal change<br/>flips the test, and undoing it flips it back<br/>5 Fix: a normal task, scope = the proven files<br/>6 Keep: the reproduction joins the permanent suite<br/>No reproduction, no fix. Each stage has a cap<br/>Hypotheses are logged. The same experiment is refused<br/>Past the cap: ask for a recording or HAR, or ship logging behind a flag"]
        is_INV --> is_LOC["Choose by evidence<br/>Used to work, and a good commit exists: git bisect run<br/>One engine only: differential run, compare network, cookies, console<br/>Intermittent: many runs, jitter, traces of pass and fail<br/>Server-side: correlation ID, temporary spans<br/>Data-dependent: shrink the input to the smallest failing case"]
        is_LOC --> is_SAFARI["Safari logout, as specified<br/>WebKit: cookie missing after the checkout redirect<br/>Chromium keeps it. SameSite=Strict is dropped on the way back<br/>Lax flips the test. Revert flips it back<br/>Fix scope is the session file. A reviewer checks the auth rules"]
        is_SAFARI --> is_FIXOK{"Does the fix touch the proven mechanism?"}
        is_FIXOK -->|Only a new guard, null check or try/catch| is_FLAG["Flag it. Two tests must pass: the symptom, and the mechanism<br/>Reverting the fix must fail both. reviewer asks: cause, or cover?"]
        is_FIXOK -->|Yes| is_KEEP["Reproduction stays. Full regression runs"]
        is_KIND -->|Yes, a normal task| is_NORMAL["Ordinary leaf task. This document does not apply"]
        is_SWEEP["A sweep changes a symbol, dependency or pattern across features,<br/>or more than 15 files. It is the only owner of those paths<br/>Exclusive lease on the compiler and search result<br/>Maintenance window: drain in-flight work there, start no new work there,<br/>leave unaffected work running<br/>Branch harness/s/id from integration, landed like a feature<br/>Afterwards, briefs are rewritten from the symbol map and re-checked"]
