        kd_LIVE --> kd_WRITE["One write connection. WAL so readers do not block<br/>Workers have no database access. MCP and typed proposals only<br/>UI and exporters read a committed revision<br/>A second process is read-only: owner row, BEGIN IMMEDIATE, and a file lock<br/>Option A and hybrid writers were rejected: enforcement would sit in foreign code"]
        kd_WRITE --> kd_FAST["Bookkeeping only. Model calls, Git and exports are outside the transaction<br/>Group commit every few milliseconds. One savepoint per request<br/>Heartbeats stay in memory. Token streams are not stored<br/>Bounded queues. Telemetry yields to task transitions<br/>Target: 50 simulated workers, p99 under 50 ms"]
        kd_FAST --> kd_SAFE{"What could go wrong?"}
        kd_SAFE -->|Busy or a failed idempotent transaction| kd_RETRY["BEGIN IMMEDIATE. Retry the whole transaction"]
        kd_SAFE -->|Two claim the same task| kd_COND["One conditional update. Success is exactly one row changed. Epoch increments"]
        kd_SAFE -->|Submit versus expiry| kd_EPOCH["Valid only if the epoch matches at commit<br/>A submission that arrived in time is not expired for queue delay"]
