    subgraph su_SRC["Budget stops, undo, coming back, and infer or ask · stops-undo-and-reentry.mmd"]
      direction TB
        su_CP["A checkpoint at every turn boundary<br/>WIP commit on refs/harness/checkpoints<br/>Attempt branch harness/t/task/attempt<br/>Session reference: Codex thread, Claude session, Cursor agent, or our transcript<br/>Handoff note written by code: brief version, steps done and left,<br/>files changed, last checks, last failing check<br/>Ledger spend and reservations, settled<br/>A limit, a crash or a closed laptop loses at most the turn in progress<br/>Resume uses the runtime's own resume when it works<br/>Otherwise a fresh session gets the brief plus the labeled diff<br/>Sleep mid-turn: treat the call as unknown, resume from the checkpoint,<br/>and reconcile an ambiguous paid call before retrying"] --> su_METER{"Spend"}
        su_METER -->|50 or 80 percent| su_ALERT["Alert only. The meter turns amber. One digest item"]
        su_METER -->|90 percent| su_WIND["Wind-down. No new attempts<br/>Running attempts finish the current step<br/>A reserve stays for checkpoints and for verifying finished candidates"]
        su_METER -->|100 percent| su_STOP["Every attempt checkpoints and parks<br/>Office lights go to evening. This is not a failed task"]
        su_METER -->|Plan window closed| su_WIN["Same as stopped, with the reset time when it is known<br/>Auto-resume only if the user enabled it"]
        su_STOP --> su_CARD
        su_WIN --> su_CARD["Stop card. Each option shows its estimate first<br/>Add budget. Use cheaper models, previewing the remainder only<br/>Switch connection. Wait for the reset. Keep parked<br/>Finish by hand: export wip branches and the feature branch<br/>of what was accepted, with the handoff in the app and<br/>optionally beside the commit. Then I fixed it myself<br/>A half-done feature is never landed. Landing with a feature<br/>flag off is an explicit option, only if it was designed that way<br/>Raising the budget resumes parked tasks in priority order<br/>Nothing starts over. A retired model uses the roster fallback"]
        su_CARD --> su_UNDO["Undo a merged feature is a current-feature change, not a blind reset<br/>1 Inventory: commits, files, routes, exports, migrations, packages,<br/>env, config, jobs, and external effects<br/>2 Who else uses each piece: edges, imports, columns, later migrations<br/>3 Classify. Only this feature: remove<br/>Shared, including a feature mid-build: keep, and move ownership<br/>Data: keep. Dropping is an explicit choice, export first,<br/>and expand-then-contract<br/>A package: remove only if nothing else imports it<br/>An external effect cannot be undone. Show the receipts<br/>A compensating action, such as unregistering a webhook, is a task if possible"]
        su_UNDO --> su_HOW{"How to execute the undo"}
        su_HOW -->|One merge, and nothing later touched its files| su_FAST["Revert that merge. Run the regression<br/>Recorded as a forward revision, so it can itself be undone"]
        su_HOW -->|Otherwise| su_TASKS["Removal tasks per area, verified like any other task,<br/>then the regression of features that shared a boundary"]
        su_FAST --> su_BACK
        su_TASKS --> su_BACK["On open, before anything runs, reconcile<br/>Last revision, outbox, expired leases fenced<br/>Missing worktrees recreated from checkpoints<br/>New base commits, dirty files, branch switches, edits in worktrees<br/>Lockfile and tool versions. Tokens, reset windows, prices, models<br/>A CLI version change reruns the adapter conformance suite<br/>Each open question is rechecked against the new commits and answers"]
        su_BACK --> su_HELLO["Welcome back. Finished while away. Parked, and why<br/>Questions waiting, including one a commit may already answer<br/>Your commits, and any overlap that will refresh a task<br/>Connections. Budget left. Nothing runs until Resume<br/>Review, or open the board, still starts nothing<br/>Each question gets a recap: the decision, why it is needed,<br/>and what the new commits changed. Older than a week: re-validate<br/>Obsolete questions are retired with a note<br/>Deleted checkpoint refs: those tasks restart from the brief<br/>Finished work on integration stays. Abandoned export branches<br/>remain theirs. The feature is marked abandoned"]
        su_HELLO --> su_USE["Infer or ask, when a criterion is resolved, a worker or planner<br/>meets a missing product decision, or a steer may change one<br/>The kernel rejects a break of these rules. One object per criterion<br/>Do not invent criteria. Propose a new gap separately, with its source"]
        su_USE --> su_FOUR{"Which status is actually earned?"}
        su_FOUR -->|A current, unretracted statement<br/>establishes this exact value| su_EXPL["explicit. Cite the exact span<br/>Your own earlier summary is not evidence"]
        su_FOUR -->|A listed rule applies, and every<br/>premise is already a resolved fact| su_DER["derived. Name the rule and the premises<br/>No circular support. Never for a costly choice"]
        su_FOUR -->|The user handed this over,<br/>inside stated limits| su_DEL["delegated. Pick inside those limits<br/>Record the reason. A recommendation alone is not this"]
        su_FOUR -->|Anything else| su_MISS["missing, partial, or conflict"]
        su_EXPL --> su_RULES
        su_DER --> su_RULES
        su_DEL --> su_RULES
        su_MISS --> su_RULES["Quote, do not paraphrase. The quote must establish the value<br/>Negation and retraction win. Keep digits and negations as spoken<br/>Paid services, identity, retention, deleting data, and legal duties<br/>are explicit, or an explicit bounded delegation. Never derived<br/>One criterion at a time. Two readings is a conflict. Do not pick one<br/>In an existing repo, code is today. The request is the change"]
        su_RULES --> su_OUT{"Must a question be asked?"}
        su_OUT -->|Yes| su_ASK["One concrete question, in their words<br/>The decision, why it matters, the options,<br/>a recommendation when one is clearly safer, and something else<br/>If two readings change behavior, show both"]
        su_OUT -->|No| su_OBJ["Return id, status, value, evidence, rule, premises,<br/>delegation, missing detail and question"]
        su_ASK --> su_OBJ
        su_OBJ --> su_SELF["Before returning: a stranger would agree each explicit quote<br/>establishes that value. Every derived value names a rule and<br/>resolved premises. No costly choice is derived<br/>Nothing is credited from a retracted or superseded span"]
    end
    subgraph ec_SRC["The developer's own edits beside the harness · editor-coexistence.mmd"]
      direction TB
        ec_RULE["The checkout is the developer's. No edit, stash, reset or commit<br/>there without an explicit click. Harness work stays in its worktrees<br/>and harness branches. harness/integration is never their checkout,<br/>so dirty files on main do not block the merge queue<br/>Nothing they wrote is discarded. A revert is a forward commit<br/>A human-owned worktree is never deleted without asking"] --> ec_WATCH["A watcher on the checkout, ignoring dependency and build folders,<br/>plus git status and ref checks<br/>Files no active task touches: say nothing<br/>package.json or the lockfile: offer to include it<br/>A new base commit: a digest item, then a base sync<br/>A branch switch: the status bar updates. The landing target stays<br/>A rebase or merge in progress: landing waits<br/>Edits inside a running worktree: same three choices as an overlap"]
        ec_WATCH --> ec_CLASS{"What did they touch?"}
        ec_CLASS -->|A file inside an active write scope| ec_OVER{"Overlap"}
        ec_CLASS -->|An uncommitted dependency change| ec_DEP{"Include it so workers can use it?"}
        ec_CLASS -->|Something else from the watch list| ec_SYNC
        ec_OVER -->|Take over| ec_TAKE["The worker stops at its next boundary<br/>WIP is a checkpoint. The task becomes human-owned"]
        ec_OVER -->|Keep both| ec_BOTH["The worker continues. On landing, merge with their committed<br/>version and resolve or report the conflicts"]
        ec_OVER -->|Ignore| ec_IGN["No change. Do not repeat this notice for this file, this session"]
        ec_DEP -->|Commit and include| ec_INC["Commit with the developer as author. It becomes base<br/>The integrator reconciles it with open dependency intents"]
        ec_DEP -->|Not now| ec_NOINC["Workers do not see the new package"]
        ec_BOTH --> ec_SYNC
        ec_IGN --> ec_SYNC
        ec_INC --> ec_SYNC
        ec_NOINC --> ec_SYNC
        ec_TAKE --> ec_OWN
        ec_SYNC["A new base commit is merged into harness/integration<br/>Recheck the changed files. Refresh in-flight tasks whose inputs changed<br/>A conflict with a running task goes to its owner as a normal revision<br/>Their commits are the new truth, and are never rewritten<br/>A force-push rebuilds integration from the new base.<br/>Tasks whose base vanished resume from checkpoints<br/>Deleting a file a finished feature added is reported, and asked about<br/>Fixing an already accepted task is a normal commit, then a recheck"] --> ec_LAND{"Bring integration onto their branch?<br/>Predict with merge-tree first. Auto-land is off"}
        ec_LAND -->|Not checked out, or clean| ec_FF["Fast-forward or a merge commit, as settings chose"]
        ec_LAND -->|Dirty files this landing does not touch| ec_SAFE["Git can update and leave those files<br/>Proceed only if auto-land is on. Otherwise ask once"]
        ec_LAND -->|Dirty files this landing does touch| ec_CARD["Never touch the tree"]
        ec_LAND -->|Rebase, merge or conflicts| ec_WAIT["Wait, and recheck when it finishes"]
        ec_CARD --> ec_C2{"Explicit click"}
        ec_C2 -->|Commit my edits first| ec_CMT["Show the diff. Commit with them as author. Then land"]
        ec_C2 -->|Land later| ec_LATER["Leave it"]
        ec_C2 -->|Stash, land, restore| ec_STASH["Say that restore may conflict. Run only on this click<br/>Never stash silently"]
        ec_C2 -->|Show me how| ec_SELF["They land it themselves"]
        ec_WATCH -.->|Or they take Fix it myself, or say so in chat| ec_FIX
        ec_FIX{"I fixed it myself. How did it start?"}
        ec_FIX -->|Card on a failed or held task| ec_OWN
        ec_FIX -->|Chat: I fixed this task| ec_OWN
        ec_FIX -->|A commit touches that write scope| ec_SUG["Suggest: verify it as that task?"]
        ec_SUG --> ec_OWN["Human-owned. The worker stops. WIP stays on a checkpoint ref<br/>Work in that task's worktree, or in their own checkout<br/>Editing is normal. The harness stays out of the way<br/>I'm done, or a chat message, collects the work<br/>Worktree: the harness commits, developer as author<br/>Own checkout: they pick the commits, prefilled from the scope"]
        ec_OWN --> ec_VER["The same clean verifier. The same locked checks<br/>The same held-back cases"]
        ec_VER --> ec_PASS{"Result"}
        ec_PASS -->|Pass| ec_ACC["Accepted. Author is the developer. Dependents unlock<br/>The node records acceptedBy human, the commit and the receipt<br/>The office shows the CEO's stamp"]
        ec_PASS -->|Fail| ec_FAIL{"Next"}
        ec_FAIL -->|Keep fixing| ec_OWN
        ec_FAIL -->|This test is wrong| ec_PROD["A product decision. Change the expectation, with an impact preview<br/>Not a quiet edit of the test"]
        ec_FAIL -->|Accept anyway| ec_OVR["Record the override and the reason<br/>Dependents see a warning. It is in the final summary"]
        ec_ACC --> ec_AFTER["If an export or a schema changed: compatible is done.<br/>Incompatible consumers are re-briefed, and the preview shows the impact<br/>Files outside the task's scope are listed: record them on their own,<br/>attach them to this task, or leave them unrecorded<br/>After days away, re-entry reconciliation runs before anything starts"]
    end
