  subgraph CH_10["10 · Shipping and moving projects"]
    direction TB
    subgraph sd_SRC["Push, CI, deploy and live migrations · ship-and-deploy.mmd"]
      direction TB
        sd_RULE["Nothing leaves the laptop without a rule<br/>Push, PR, deploy, migration, env sync, DNS and webhooks are effects:<br/>intent, approval, idempotency key and receipt<br/>The harness pushes harness branches and opens PRs<br/>It does not push main unless the developer turns that on<br/>for a repo with no branch protection<br/>Production deploy, live migration and DNS need approval each time<br/>Preview and staging can be automatic"] --> sd_REMOTE["Detect origin. GitHub first. GitLab later<br/>Device OAuth, or an existing gh login, in the vault<br/>Read branch protection and required checks<br/>Default is PR mode. Direct mode pushes a branch the developer names"]
        sd_REMOTE --> sd_DONE{"Feature reaches DONE<br/>Each PR, CI run and deploy is a ship_runs row"}
        sd_DONE --> sd_PUSH["One push of harness/f/feature. Not one push per task<br/>Open a draft PR from the graph: requirements, checks, migrations,<br/>new dependencies, choices made for them, links to the plan<br/>The structure needs no model. A summary paragraph is optional"]
        sd_PUSH --> sd_CI{"GitHub Actions"}
        sd_CI -->|Green| sd_READY["Mark the PR ready. Land as settings say<br/>Required reviewers: wait. Never bypass them"]
        sd_CI -->|Red| sd_TRIAGE["Read failed logs. Patterns first, then a small model<br/>Platform difference: repair, and reproduce in the Tier D container<br/>Missing secret: a human step. Never paste it into code<br/>Flaky: re-run once, then the test owner<br/>Real regression: repair task to the owning feature<br/>Runner or quota: wait. No repair task<br/>The worker sees the failing lines. Same fingerprint, 3 pushes, then the developer<br/>Phase 0's CI workflow runs the same gates on Linux and Windows"]
        sd_TRIAGE -->|Repair pushed| sd_PUSH
        sd_PUSH --> sd_QUEUE["One GitHub queue per account<br/>Content-creating calls stay under 80 a minute and 500 an hour<br/>Polling is conditional and backs off from 30 seconds to 5 minutes<br/>retry-after and x-ratelimit-reset are obeyed<br/>Repeated secondary limits pause the queue and show in the cockpit"]
        sd_READY --> sd_DEPLOY{"Which environment?"}
        sd_QUEUE --> sd_DEPLOY
        sd_DEPLOY -->|Preview, per PR| sd_PREV["Automatic. Test secrets. A disposable or branched database"]
        sd_DEPLOY -->|Staging| sd_STG["Automatic after the PR is ready, if staging is configured"]
        sd_DEPLOY -->|Production| sd_PROD["Explicit approval, with the plan shown"]
        sd_PREV --> sd_ADAPT
        sd_STG --> sd_ADAPT
        sd_PROD --> sd_ADAPT["One adapter interface: probe, plan, deploy, status, logs,<br/>promote, rollback, syncEnv<br/>v1: Vercel and Docker over SSH<br/>Railway, Fly.io, Render and AWS come later. No hosting yet is a discovery question. Nothing is created unasked"]
        sd_ADAPT --> sd_ENV["Vault holds values per environment<br/>syncEnv shows names only, and production needs approval<br/>Production values are never pulled back for tests"]
        sd_ENV --> sd_MIG["0 Rehearse on a copy or a restored staging backup. Automatic<br/>1 Backup or point-in-time recovery. Must succeed<br/>2 Expand only: new tables, nullable columns, concurrent indexes<br/>3 Deploy the app, which can read old and new<br/>4 Batched backfill, with progress and pause<br/>5 Contract in a later release, separately approved, export offered<br/>A destructive migration cannot skip rehearsal and backup<br/>A long lock switches to an online plan, or asks for a window"]
        sd_MIG --> sd_CHECK{"After deploy"}
        sd_CHECK --> sd_HEALTH["Health and build ID. Smoke journeys with a test account<br/>Watch errors for 10 minutes"]
