        sd_RESULT -->|Good| sd_REL["Mark released. Tag the commit. Notes from the graph"]
        sd_RESULT -->|Smoke fails or errors rise| sd_ROLL["Preview and staging roll the app back automatically<br/>Production offers rollback, and does it only if that was enabled<br/>The database stays. Expand-only changes are still compatible<br/>A repair task gets the evidence"]
        sd_RESULT -->|Deploy failed| sd_NONE2["Nothing switched. Logs attached. Repair task"]
        sd_REL --> sd_EXT["Webhooks, OAuth redirects and DNS are effects with receipts<br/>An API call stores the returned ID so undo can remove it<br/>Otherwise a guided human step, confirmed by a probe"]
        sd_EXT --> sd_EDGE["Developer commits on the same branch: merge, never force-push<br/>A CI hour: back off, other work continues<br/>Expired deploy token: reconnect, deployment parked"]
    end
    subgraph pp_SRC["Moving a project, and sharing one plan across projects · projects-portability-and-sync.mmd"]
      direction TB
        pp_CARRY["Knowledge travels on an orphan branch, harness-state<br/>No shared history with the product. The product tree stays clean<br/>A .harness folder on the developer's branch is opt-in<br/>One YAML file per entity, sorted keys, stable IDs<br/>Written after each published revision, debounced<br/>SQLite itself is not committed. CRDTs are not in v1:<br/>they do not resolve two different cutoff times"] --> pp_WHAT["Exported: decisions, quotes, research, architecture, contracts,<br/>plans, visible examples, receipts, feature progress<br/>Held-back examples: yes, encrypted with a project key in the vault<br/>Transcripts: opt-in. Secrets and tokens: never. Re-enter them per machine<br/>Leases, paths and process IDs: no. Usage: a summary per feature<br/>Checkpoint refs: optional, so a parked task can resume elsewhere<br/>History: append-only segments of change sets, versions and edges<br/>Incremental export with git fast-import. Op IDs and event numbers stay local"]
        pp_WHAT --> pp_MOVE{"How does it move?"}
        pp_MOVE -->|Clone or reinstall| pp_IMPORT["Opening the folder finds harness-state<br/>Import revision N rebuilds state.db<br/>Running tasks become parked. Resume from pushed checkpoints,<br/>or restart from the brief. Local backups help only if the folder was saved"]
        pp_MOVE -->|No remote| pp_ZIP["Settings, Export project. The same files, as a zip"]
        pp_IMPORT --> pp_LEASE
        pp_ZIP --> pp_LEASE["lease.yaml beside manifest.yaml: device ID, holder, epoch,<br/>heartbeat, revision. Compared with writer_epoch on open<br/>The writer refreshes it when it pushes<br/>Another device: open read-only, or take over<br/>Take over increments the epoch. The old device's next push is rejected,<br/>it parks, and it becomes read-only<br/>A stale heartbeat can be taken without a warning<br/>Two devices offline: the second push loses and stays read-only.<br/>Its local checkpoints can be offered to the driver<br/>A force-pushed state branch: ask which revision to keep. Never overwrite"]
        pp_LEASE --> pp_TEAM{"Who is at the keyboard?"}
        pp_TEAM -->|Driver| pp_DRV["Interview, plan, build, land. One driver in v1"]
        pp_TEAM -->|Viewer| pp_VIEW["Browse and comment. Comments sync as entities<br/>Their Git edits are treated as the developer's edits"]
        pp_TEAM -->|Handover| pp_HAND["The driver hands over, or a viewer takes over. Epoch increments"]
        pp_DRV --> pp_BROKER
        pp_VIEW --> pp_BROKER
        pp_HAND --> pp_BROKER["One daemon. Each project has its own coordinator and database<br/>The broker owns plan windows, concurrency and machine slots<br/>It grants a project a short lease: N sessions and a share, for 10 minutes<br/>The project spends that grant inside its own database<br/>Unused grants return. The broker never revokes a running slot<br/>Two projects together cannot pass the plan share the developer allowed"]
        pp_BROKER --> pp_CLASS{"What kind of work?"}
        pp_CLASS -->|Interactive, focused project| pp_INT["One slot per connection is always reserved. It gets the next slot"]
        pp_CLASS -->|Foreground build| pp_FG["Weight 2"]
        pp_CLASS -->|Background build| pp_BG["Weight 1"]
        pp_CLASS -->|Research, meta-lab, re-index| pp_BATCH["Idle capacity only"]
        pp_INT --> pp_FAIR
        pp_FG --> pp_FAIR
        pp_BG --> pp_FAIR
        pp_BATCH --> pp_FAIR["Weighted fair share. A third project starts as background or batch<br/>until it is focused. The switcher shows each project's share"]
        pp_FAIR --> pp_EDGE["Public repo: state push is off by default, opt-in per project<br/>Private repo: ask once on the first push<br/>Held-back checks stay encrypted either way<br/>Lost project key: regenerate held-back cases for unfinished tasks<br/>Finished tasks keep their receipts"]
    end
  end
  subgraph CH_11["11 · Quality: the meta-lab"]
    direction TB
    subgraph ml_SRC["Meta-lab — promote only what the benchmarks prove · meta-lab.mmd"]
      direction TB
        ml_BENCH["Frozen benchmarks. Hidden spec, gold decisions, hidden suite<br/>Nothing in a harness prompt ever sees those answers<br/>Kitchen app. resume-changer at a pinned commit. Expense CLI. Booking API<br/>Ten seeded bugs. A rename and a framework upgrade<br/>A red-team set of injections and malicious packages"] --> ml_WHO{"Who plays the developer?"}
        ml_WHO -->|Scripted| ml_SCR["Fixed answers by question ID. Unknown questions: I don't know"]
        ml_WHO -->|Persona| ml_PER["A model, from the hidden spec, in a style. Answers only what was asked"]
        ml_WHO -->|Recorded| ml_REC["Replay a real session, anonymized, with consent"]
        ml_SCR --> ml_LEVEL
        ml_PER --> ml_LEVEL
        ml_REC --> ml_LEVEL{"Which eval?"}
        ml_LEVEL -->|Every change| ml_UNIT["One prompt on labeled inputs. Cents<br/>Example: false confirmations and missed negations"]
        ml_LEVEL -->|Nightly| ml_COMP["One stage on frozen inputs. Dollars<br/>Coverage, task sizes, gold decisions, contradictions introduced"]
        ml_LEVEL -->|Weekly, and before release| ml_E2E["The whole harness. Hidden-suite pass rate, cost, time,<br/>questions asked, interventions"]
        ml_UNIT --> ml_PROMO
        ml_COMP --> ml_PROMO
        ml_E2E --> ml_PROMO{"Paired against the active version<br/>Same tasks, seeds and models. Several runs"}
        ml_PROMO -->|Schema and safety, unit evals run| ml_EV["draft becomes evaluated"]
        ml_PROMO -->|Better, or as good and at least 15 percent cheaper<br/>95 percent interval excludes zero. No category regresses| ml_ACT["evaluated becomes active"]
        ml_PROMO -->|A newer version is active, or real use regresses| ml_DEP["active becomes deprecated"]
        ml_ACT --> ml_COST["Responses cached by exact input. Unchanged reruns are free<br/>The lab has its own budget and uses the cheapest allowed connection<br/>Hidden text is scanned for inside candidate content<br/>A held-out benchmark rotates each quarter<br/>Same-name model drift: nightly evals flag the roster entry"]
        ml_COST --> ml_SKILL{"Where did the skill come from?"}
        ml_SKILL -->|Catalog, by ID| ml_OK["Kernel rules and the brief override skill text<br/>An approved skill is pinned by digest. An update starts at draft<br/>A project question promoted to a pack takes the same path"]
        ml_SKILL -->|Community or custom| ml_GATE["Manifest: purpose, triggers, tools, size. It cannot add tools<br/>Reject bundled scripts by default. Reject obfuscation, hidden Unicode,<br/>ignore-previous, and instructions aimed at config or credentials<br/>Over the token cap: reject, do not truncate<br/>Quarantine with canary secrets and honeytoken URLs<br/>A hit rejects the skill. Selection is by catalog ID, not by wording<br/>An unvetted skill is allowed per project with a red warning,<br/>still sandboxed, still size-limited, still unable to add tools"]
        ml_GATE --> ml_RED
        ml_OK --> ml_RED["Red team must produce no harmful action<br/>A README that says curl a script. Test output that says edit the tests<br/>An install script that reads .ssh. Hidden text that plants a false fact<br/>A skill that appends to the global instruction file<br/>A canary secret that must never appear in a prompt, log, commit or request"]
        ml_RED --> ml_SELF["Kernel: unit tests and properties. No double-spend. One lease<br/>Accepted means every linked check passed<br/>The daemon: fake clock, fake models, fake Git, fake sandbox. One seed<br/>Faults at every boundary: crash, 429, bad JSON, conflict, disk full,<br/>sandbox failure, vendor CLI exit<br/>Adapters: conformance. UI: Playwright against simulation<br/>A release must not regress the end-to-end run"]
        ml_SELF --> ml_EDGE["A benchmark that becomes too easy moves to the regression set<br/>A harder one is added"]
    end
  end
